// ─── structure/no-plain-export-in-server-fn-module ────────────────────
//
// Tag:      structure
// Mechanism: GritQL (per-file, real-time)
// Blocking: Yes
//
// Prevents: A plain top-level `export function` co-located in a file that
//           also defines a createServerFn. Same class as
//           structure/middleware-colocation: the TanStack Start compiler
//           strips only the createServerFn `.handler()` BODIES from the
//           client bundle — a sibling plain export ships to the browser
//           verbatim, dragging its imports with it. The day such a helper
//           touches a server-only module (DB client, node: builtin) the
//           whole chain lands in the client bundle and the app crashes at
//           runtime ("X is not defined" / an externalized-module error).
//
//           This is the per-file GUARD for a bundle-graph problem GritQL
//           can't see across files. Its cross-file complement is
//           api/barrel-purity — whose server-fn-boundary short-circuit is
//           only SOUND when server-fn modules hold server functions +
//           types and nothing else. This rule enforces exactly that, so
//           the two are designed to be adopted together.
//
//           The fix is structural: move server-only helpers to a
//           `.server.ts` sibling, whose suffix is a hard client-import
//           fence (via import protection).
//
// Applies:  All src/** files that contain createServerFn calls.
//           Excludes test files, scripts, and *.server.ts (already fenced
//           off the client, so a plain export there is safe).
//
// Error:    "Plain `export function` in a module that also defines a
//            createServerFn ships to the client bundle (only handler
//            bodies are stripped). Move server-only helpers to a
//            .server.ts sibling — its suffix blocks client imports."
//
// ── Adapt ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. Factory name:
//    If your framework uses a different server-function factory,
//    replace `createServerFn` with the correct identifier.
//
// 2. Server-only fence suffix:
//    This template assumes `.server.ts` is the import-protected suffix
//    (TanStack Start convention). If your project fences server-only
//    modules differently, update the exclusion regex and the error.
//
// 3. Arrow-function exports:
//    This template flags `export function` / `export async function`
//    declarations — the common leak shape. It does NOT flag
//    `export const foo = () => {...}`; `export const fooFn =
//    createServerFn()...` (a call expression) must stay legal, and
//    distinguishing a plain arrow from a server-fn chain adds arms for
//    little gain. Tighten only if arrow-declared helpers leak in practice.
//
// 4. The four arms below cover function/async × with/without a
//    return-type annotation. A `): T {` return type is a distinct node
//    sitting BETWEEN the params and the body — a snippet with no slot for
//    it (`($_args) { $... }`) silently fails to match any annotated
//    function, the most common reason this rule appears to "do nothing."
//    Keep all four arms.
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

file(name=$filename, body=$program) where {
    // --- Global exclusions (shared across all rules) ---
    ! $filename <: r".*\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*\.integration\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*__tests__.*|.*src/test/.*",
    ! $filename <: r".*/scripts/.*",
    ! $filename <: r".*\.server\.[tj]sx?$",

    // Only check files that expose a client-imported server-fn stub.
    $program <: contains `createServerFn`,

    // Flag any plain exported function declaration in that same file.
    $program <: contains bubble or {
        `export function $name($_args): $_ret { $... }`,
        `export async function $name($_args): $_ret { $... }`,
        `export function $name($_args) { $... }`,
        `export async function $name($_args) { $... }`
    } as $leak where {
        register_diagnostic(
            span = $leak,
            message = "Plain `export function` in a module that also defines a createServerFn ships to the client bundle (only handler bodies are stripped). Move server-only helpers to a .server.ts sibling — its suffix blocks client imports."
        )
    }
}
